{"step_index":151,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T02:09:42Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-27T02:09:42Z\nCompleted At: 2026-10-27T02:09:42Z\nShowing lines 1-60 of 149\n1: # LLM session export → `/home/jeremy/.notebooklm-sources`\n2: \n3: The scheduler captures conversations **and tool calls** into local raw files\n4: grouped by model. Its independent local capture continues when remote sync is\n5: blocked. The optional formatted exporter remains a separate consumer; its text\n6: is labelled fallback history when an original transcript is unavailable.\n7: \n8: The received `notebook-sources-sync` service selects the existing human session\n9: and `/run/mount/3tchedFS` mount explicitly. It uses the mount's declared operator\n10: UID 0; canonical method admission retains the bound session and its grants.\n11: Its code comes from the received service component; project documents come from\n12: `/srv/git/odbus-verified`. Current local raw files and their source/hash inventory\n13: are in `~/.notebooklm-sources/.local-capture/{chunks,plan.json}`. The frozen upload\n14: plan and durable journal remain separately in `.grouped-sync`.\n15: There is no direct `nlm`, gRPC or unauthenticated D-Bus fallback in sync.\n16: \n17: The configured history roots are `/home/jeremy`, `/root`, and\n18: `/home/jeremy/keep`. Native history patterns and read-only conversation tables\n19: cover retained and current files. The plan records those roots; pre-recovery\n20: coverage is limited to the histories that survived. Capture files and plans\n21: remain private and readable by Jeremy even though the service reads root-owned\n22: conversation archives.\n23: \n24: Remote sync has its own protected `/etc/op-dbus/notebook-sources-sync.enabled`\n25: flag. It does not use the chatbot's `threetched-filesystem.enabled` opt-in.\n26: A missing owned upload journal blocks remote writes while local capture keeps\n27: running. Restoring notebook associations requires explicit operator\n28: reconciliation; matching titles alone are not automatically adopted. The\n29: 2026-10-12 repair reconnected 62 unique existing collector notebooks from an\n30: admitted account inventory. Their 913 existing sources remain unmanaged and\n31: retained. `OPDBUS_NOTEBOOK_CAPTURE_EPOCH=20261012-recovery` identifies the new\n32: recovery batch, so processed legacy content is not adopted as raw-byte proof.\n33: \n34: The client resumes the exact saved plan before capturing later appends. It\n35: records mutation intent before dispatch and retains receipts; an unknown\n36: outcome is not permission to repeat an upload or deletion. Old owned sources\n37: remain until replacements are readable. Exit 0 means the cycle completed,\n38: 2 means processing or bounded work remains, and other exits mean failure.\n39: The service publishes that distinction, a blocked reason, and the independent\n40: local-capture result in\n41: `/run/opdbus/notebook-sync/status.json`; a running process alone is not proof\n42: of synchronization. The current component's deployment and live evidence are\n43: recorded under `notebook-local-recovery-20261012` in `HANDOFF.md`.\n44: \n45: ## Storage reality\n46: \n47: | CLI | Where history lives | Session lifetime |\n48: | --- | --- | --- |\n49: | **OpenCode** | SQLite `~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db` (`session` / `message` / `part`) | **Persistent** (DB rows grow across runs) |\n50: | **Kilo** | SQLite `~/.local/share/kilo/kilo.db` (same shape) | **Persistent** |\n51: | **Codex** | SQLite `~/.codex/state_5.sqlite` + rollout JSONL | Per thread; rollouts grow |\n52: | **AGY** | `conversations/*.db` + `brain/*/transcript.jsonl` | Per conversation |\n53: | **Cursor** | `agent-transcripts/**/*.jsonl` (+ thin `store.db` meta) | Per agent id |\n54: | **Factory / droid** | `~/.factory/sessions/**/*.jsonl` | **Persistent** (same JSONL append) |\n55: | **Grok** | `~/.grok/sessions/**/chat_history.jsonl` | Per session dir |\n56: | **Claude** | `~/.claude/projects/**/*.jsonl` | Per session file |\n57: \n58: Because **factory** and **opencode** (and kilo) do not “close” a session on CLI exit, exit hooks must **re-read the store** and only rewrite when content changes.\n59: \n60: ## Commands"}
